Chapter: CodexZigRingHarness

Section: Halt

 The driver this stands in for does not emit when the bag has errors:
 opening.codex:1676-1678 prints the codegen error header and the notices,
 and then `if bag-has-errors (fe.bag) then print-line-uni "CODEGEN-HALTED:
 errors in bag; no IR emitted"`. Without this gate a file reading `this is
 not codex at all` produces 36,697 bytes of plausible zig and exit 0, and so
 does a program calling a function that does not exist -- measured, both. For
 a tool handed to other people, the first thing they will feed it is a
 program with a mistake in it.

 The bags are the ones the driver merges, reached from what the frontend
 already binds: lex errors from `toks.errors` (opening.codex:449 wraps the
 same list), the parse bag from `doc.parse-bag` (:485), the resolve bag from
 `rr.bag`, and the type checker's from `cr.state.bag` -- which is what
 `check-bag0` at :620 merges. The PRINTERS are not reachable: they live in
 opening.codex, which cannot be bundled beside a harness defining `opening`,
 so this prints the count and the first error rather than the driver's full
 report.

 CODEGEN-HALTED is the marker build.py refuses on by name, in the two
 places a transpile is read: the bare-metal arm and the self arm.

  czg-halted : List Diagnostic -> Text
  czg-halted (es) =
   let n = list-length es
   in let e0 = list-at es 0
   in "CODEGEN-HALTED: " & show n & " error(s); no zig emitted; first CDX" & show (e0.code) & " " & (e0.message) & "
"

Section: Roots

 opening.codex:1316, copied because that chapter cannot ride along.

  czg-emit-roots : List Text
  czg-emit-roots = ["opening", "vb-capacity-auto", "vb-read-auto", "vb-write-auto", "fat16-servicer-read", "fat16-servicer-write"]

Section: Driver

 The same pipeline as CodexZigHarness behind a different front door. That
 harness reads `/dev/stdin`, which is a hosted path and means nothing to a
 program with no OS under it. This one reads its unit exactly the way the
 seed's own driver does (opening.codex:2188-2189) -- `read-file-uni mode`,
 then `utf8-to-cce` -- and answers on ZigPlugRing's wire, a SIZE: line then
 the payload as raw CCE bytes.

 Taking the driver's intake rather than ZigPlugRing's is the correction that
 made this work, and the reason is the encoding. `read-serial-cce` converts
 NOTHING: it copies raw bytes until a NUL, because its caller is a wire that
 already speaks CCE, which is true of an IR file the seed emitted and false
 of Codex source. Fed plain source it produced 37,688 bytes of bare prelude
 -- a parse of garbage -- rather than failing. `utf8-to-cce` is the
 conversion, it lives in Emit/X86_64State.codex, and this bundle already
 carries that chapter. The alternative was a host-side unicode-to-CCE
 encoder, which would have had to reimplement upstream's table for the five
 non-ASCII characters in the subject (é, Γ, ε, τ, ⊢) and would have been a
 fork of an encoding.

 The point of it is to find out whether the bootstrap needs three guests or
 two. Today the front end runs in one guest (seed -> IR text) and the emitter
 runs in another (ring plug -> zig). This harness puts both in ONE kernel, so
 the whole thing becomes: compile codexzig to a kernel, then use it to
 transpile codexzig.

 The open question is heap, not correctness. One guest now holds the source,
 the AST, the IR and the emitted text at once, in a bump allocator that never
 frees, and the seed dies silently above 3072 MB.

 The IR text round trip is kept, and for the same reason CodexZigHarness
 keeps it: the wire DERIVES a record's implicit type parameters as it
 serialises, so a direct hand-off emits zig that does not compile.

  opening : [Console, FileSystem] Nothing = act
    mode-result <- read-line
    when mode-result
     is Just (mode) -> czr-emit mode
     is None -> print-line-uni "CODEXZIGRING-FAIL: no mode line"
  end

  czr-emit : Text -> [Console, FileSystem] Nothing
  czr-emit (mode) = act
    src-raw <- read-file-uni mode
    let src = utf8-to-cce src-raw
    in let mountain-base = init-phase-allocator
    in let deck-base = __heap-save
    in let deck-set = __deck-set deck-base
    in let deck-adv = __heap-advance 536870912
    in let toks = tokenize src 1
    in let scan = scan-document (make-parse-state (toks.tokens) src)
    in let assignments = build-all-assignments src (scan.def-headers) 0 []
    in let colliding = find-colliding-names assignments
    in let renames = build-global-rename-table assignments colliding
    in let doc = parse-document (make-parse-state (toks.tokens) src) 0
    in let dr = desugar-document src doc (doc.chapter-title) 0
    in let ch0 = dr.dr-chapter
    in let ch = scope-achapter ch0 colliding assignments 0
    in let rr = resolve-chapter ch colliding assignments 0
    in let cr = check-chapter ch renames colliding assignments 0
    in let resolved-et = for e in (sort-expr-types ((cr.state).expr-types)) -> ExprTypeEntry { key = e.key, ty = deep-resolve (cr.state) (e.ty) }
    in let cst = __record-set (cr.state) "expr-types" resolved-et
    in let resolved-env = for b in ((cr.env).bindings) -> TypeBinding { name = b.name, bound-type = deep-resolve cst (b.bound-type) }
    in let bound = for b in (sort-bindings (cr.types & resolved-env)) -> TypeBinding { name = b.name, bound-type = deep-resolve cst (b.bound-type) }
    in let ir-raw = lower-chapter ch bound cst (rr.ctor-names) renames colliding assignments 0
    in let passed = run-ir-pipeline default-ir-pipeline ir-raw False
    in let ir0 = passed.chapter
    in let ir = lift-lambdas ir0 0
    in let czg-bag = bag-merge-all [bag-from-list (toks.errors), doc.parse-bag, rr.bag, cr.state.bag]
    in if bag-has-errors czg-bag then print-text (czg-halted (bag-errors czg-bag))
    else let meta = IRTextMeta {
      chapter-title = ch.chapter-title,
      prose = ch.prose,
      section-titles = ch.section-titles,
      ctor-names = rr.ctor-names,
      prose-blocks = ch.prose-blocks,
      annotations = ch.annotations,
      ground-effects = ch.ground-effects
    }
    in let ir-text = emit-ir-chapter (ir-prune-unreachable-roots ir czg-emit-roots) meta (ch.type-defs)
    in let parsed = parse-ir-chapter ir-text
    in let zig = emit-zig-chapter (parsed.chapter) (parsed.type-defs)
    in act
      print-line-uni ("SIZE:" & show (text-length zig))
      print-text zig
      print-line-uni ""
      print-line-uni ("CODEXZIGRING-DONE src=" & show (text-length src))
    end
  end
